! The Three-Lineage Convergence

Three magic-system designs, independently derived across four decades, factor magic the same way
— and their differences teach the SDM thirteen exactly where it stands. Read alongside
[[arcana-model|lar:///ha.ka.ba/sdm/docs/arcana-model]]; grown from the 2026-08-13 lens session.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-three>>

!! The Three Factorings

* ''Ars Magica (1987):'' a ''pure product grammar'' — five techniques (Creo · Intellego · Muto ·
  Perdo · Rego) × ten forms = fifty cells, setting-agnostic, no cell privileged. Verbs times
  themes, immaculate and unhistoried.
* ''Mage: the Ascension (1993):'' ''nine rated dimensions'' — a mage rides as a vector (Forces 3,
  Correspondence 2…), an effect as a point the vector must dominate. First edition blended
  spheres and cross-Tradition rotes as the normal case; later editions retreated to single-sphere
  filing and the conjunctional culture thinned.
* ''SDM (this canon):'' thirteen rooms — a verb basis ''warped by the setting's metaphysical
  geography''. Three rooms carry a fused form (shape×life · bind×death's-border · cross×the-edge)
  and the fusions sit precisely at the cosmology's scars: the rewritten flesh, the stabbed Death,
  the maelstrom edge.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/mappings>>

!! The Mappings (evidence of convergence)

* ''AD&D's eight schools'' route into the thirteen without remainder — abjuration splits
  Battle/ECM on the before/after-signal law; necromancy splits Deathless/Biomancy on which side
  of death the flesh sits. Both splits principled.
* ''Mage's nine spheres'' map near-bijectively onto the nine-plus-one power rooms:
  Correspondence + Time → the Void edge · Prime → Mana · Life → Biomancy · Mind → Psychic ·
  Spirit → Summoning/Deathless · Forces → Battle · Matter → Artifice · Entropy → Mana/Battle.
* ''The procedural quartet re-derives in Ars:'' Parma/Penetration = ECM resolution (the contest
  measures the will behind the signal, never the payload — both systems cut it the same way) ·
  vis = Mana with a supply chain · the seasonal laboratory = Ritual Mechanics at year-scale ·
  the Limits of Magic = the Ascension ceiling as negative theology.
* ''Psionics enters at 0e itself'' (Eldritch Wizardry) and needs no fourteenth room — Psychic
  Warfare takes the powers, Mana takes the point economy.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-lessons>>

!! What Each Lens Teaches

* ''From Ars:'' the verb×theme factoring works — and a PURE grammar reads as a conlang. The SDM
  thirteen limp in three places on purpose: ''the taxonomy is the archaeology.'' The irregular
  rooms are the oldest wounds. Do not regularize them.
* ''From Mage 1e:'' blends must stay first-class or the culture stops blending (the blend-law in
  the arcana model). And the rating-vector — character standing as a vector over the arcana —
  hands Ascension its sphere-dot pattern: rank tags as dots, initiation as buying the next one
  with a rite.
* ''From the RAW lineage both descend from:'' Mage asked "what if belief were load-bearing?" and
  made it a tragedy; Elyncia asks the same and makes it a maintenance schedule. Paradox becomes
  the Danger Roll; consensus becomes the noosphere, tended rather than enforced.
* ''For the witness lanes:'' Ars 5e (extraction standing at `~/Ars-Magica/work/`) and the Mage
  editions enter as witness lanes feeding the same thirteen — the guard-law's final clause,
  already proven survivable by every mapping above.

<<~/ahu>>

